{"@context":{"@vocab":"https://schema.org/","course":"identifier","wing":"isBasedOn","title":"name","principle":"abstract","skills":"keywords","lessons":"hasPart","key":"identifier","why":"description","statement":"mathExpression","address":"sameAs","skill":"keywords"},"@type":"Course","kind":"school-course","course":"CrossFormulas","wing":"CrossFormulas.lean","title":"Cross Formulas","principle":"THE LEDGER'S OWN ALGEBRA, COUNTED (the captain, 2026-09-25","skills":["cross-formulas"],"level":100,"band":"100–999 steps","rank":104,"lessons":[{"key":"the_generated_closure_partitions_into_three_kinds","name":"CLAIMED: of 610627 crosses the corpus's own integers generate, 512218 are forced by an operator's algebra, 452 are stated, and 97957 remain — and the three account for the whole, 512218 + 452 + 97957 = 610627.","statement":"(512218 + 452 + 97957 = 610627) ∧ (512218 > 5 * 97957)","address":"1b2a918f-664f-8de1-aad6-67450d393567","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"512218 + 452 + 97957 = 610627 \\quad\\land\\quad 512218 > 5 \\cdot 97957","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>512218</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>452</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>97957</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>610627</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>512218</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>97957</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"the_arithmetic_alphabet_partitions_by_its_own_algebra","name":"CLAIMED: the 6 arithmetic operators the sealed formulas use split by what they do over the corpus's own integers — 2 commutative (* +), 3 forced on their diagonal (% - /), 1 neither (^) — and 2 + 3 + 1 = 6.","statement":"((2 + 3 + 1 = 6) ∧ (3 > 2)) ∧ (2 > 1)","address":"23ada59a-4cdb-8039-94c3-cdd81827a5c2","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"2 + 3 + 1 = 6 \\quad\\land\\quad 3 > 2 \\quad\\land\\quad 2 > 1","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"the_same_arithmetic_answers_more_than_one_domain","name":"CLAIMED: 1530 formula-shaped statements carry 1458 distinct byte-strings but only 490 distinct cross contents, and 24 of those contents are sealed in more than one wing — the widest in 5. The corpus states fewer facts than statements, and the difference is where its domains meet.","statement":"((490 < 1458) ∧ (1458 < 1530)) ∧ ((490 * 3 < 1530) ∧ (5 > 2))","address":"f6f4cd96-f815-82fb-8791-fba1e09c8be7","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"490 < 1458 \\quad\\land\\quad 1458 < 1530 \\quad\\land\\quad 490 \\cdot 3 < 1530 \\quad\\land\\quad 5 > 2","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>490</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1458</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>1458</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1530</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>490</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1530</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"most_of_the_unstated_remainder_stays_inside_one_wing","name":"CLAIMED: of 97957 unstated crosses, 43044 join integers no single wing carries all three of — over two fifths and under a half, since 43044 × 5 > 97957 × 2 and 43044 × 2 < 97957.","statement":"((43044 * 5 > 97957 * 2) ∧ (43044 * 2 < 97957)) ∧ (43044 < 97957)","address":"6c181cba-f2c0-8dc7-be07-078ceb2f3f8b","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"43044 \\cdot 5 > 97957 \\cdot 2 \\quad\\land\\quad 43044 \\cdot 2 < 97957 \\quad\\land\\quad 43044 < 97957","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>43044</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>97957</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>43044</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>97957</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>43044</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>97957</mn></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"the_corpus_has_sealed_under_a_hundredth_of_its_own_closure","name":"CLAIMED: the 1530 formula-shaped statements across 115 wings are built from 779 distinct integers and state 452 crosses, against 97957 their own integers generate unstated — fewer than one in a hundred, since 452 × 100 < 97957, at between 13 and 14 formulas per wing.","statement":"((452 * 100 < 97957) ∧ (779 > 115)) ∧ ((115 * 13 < 1530) ∧ (115 * 14 > 1530))","address":"4f7121df-4f7f-8b6e-ab77-02a51908a3b2","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"452 \\cdot 100 < 97957 \\quad\\land\\quad 779 > 115 \\quad\\land\\quad 115 \\cdot 13 < 1530 \\quad\\land\\quad 115 \\cdot 14 > 1530","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>452</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>97957</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>779</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>115</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>115</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1530</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>115</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1530</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null}],"exercises":0}
